§2 body: PP non-blank 101, main 122, shared 67, only-main 55, only-PP 34
   only-main: ## Appendix E — Q, indexed and closed
   only-main: Serving PART VI — THE RECORD AND THE REACH. The book's own ignorance as a closed index — fourteen items,
   only-main: ten of them open, four ordered coordinates, one categorical fibre, E(Q) = 0 fibred by domain at the
   only-main: fourteen (§E.1.5), the domain column printed at last — and see §32.1.1 flag 2 for what a fibred
   only-main: zero is worth.
   only-main: Appendix D indexes the book's mathematics. This one indexes what the book does not know. The set has
   only-main: been recomputed six times; §E.1.1 is its lineage and §E.1.2 its current contents. The earlier states —
   only-main: nine items; eight closed at E(Q) = 0 with four entered by §12.11.7; thirteen — are kept there as history.
   only-main: ### E.1 The coordinates
   only-main: ### E.1.1 The lineage of this index, and why only one section states it
   only-main: §12.11.7 and the repairs of register 211 15 four by the tower, L and M by Appendices E and F
   only-main: E.1.2, as first listed 13 N, O and P entered, having been named and never entered
   only-main: E.1.2, current 14 R entered — |Cl(ℛ)| for Λ, register 461
   only-main: ### E.1.2 The open set as this session leaves it — ten open of 14, listed
   only-main: item question blocks obstacle cost domain
   only-main: A the Sc VI level, measured one claim nonexistent unbounded physical
   only-main: B Paschen & Götze §III, read nothing retrievable days bibliographic
   only-main: C the nine named literatures, entered nothing retrievable unbounded bibliographic
   only-main: D the Kreuzer–Skarke Hodge pairs, read one claim retrievable days computational
   only-main: F the reorderability decision problem, searched nothing buildable days mathematical
   only-main: G the complexity literature, entered nothing retrievable hours bibliographic
   only-main: H whether Sc VI has already been measured one claim retrievable days physical
   only-main: I the spectroscopic v-check per channel one claim retrievable days physical
   only-main: K the earlier bound 2J_c ≤ k, tested for containment CLOSED — — mathematical
   only-main: M Appendix F — nine stable cells, named at F.3.1 CLOSED — — computational
   only-main: N whether anyone has lattice-ordered the seniority scheme CLOSED — no; the scheme is ordered by group–subgroup chains, and Racah recorded in 1954 that
   only-main: O tree propagation retested on Λ₉′'s f–g–2S′ cycle CLOSED — — mathematical
   only-main: P the 1,442 split into independent and Ritz-derived tests one claim retrievable hours physical
   only-main: R |Cl(ℛ)| for Λ — how many closed subsets a closed index has one claim buildable unbounded mathematical
   only-main: ### E.1.3 What this index asserts, and what it recomputes
   only-main: F.3.1 establishes that a count computed from the book cannot be printed as prose, because writing the
   only-main: §12.11.3.1's rule applied here as F.3.1 applies it there — assert the law, compute the extent.
   only-main: ### E.1.4 This is an index of tractable ignorance, and it cannot say otherwise
   only-main: ### E.1.5 The fourteenth item, the column that was never printed, and the constraint it killed
   only-main: The domain column above was assigned in the code that computed E(Q) at register 256 and never
   only-main: printed; the fibration by domain that E.1.3 asserts was therefore a claim the page could not check.
   only-main: It is printed now, with the value orders the code used — blocks nothing < novelty < one claim < a
   only-main: result, obstacle retrievable < buildable < nonexistent, cost hours < days < unbounded — and the
   only-main: record's thirteen reproduce the record: E(Q) = 0 fibred, 1 unfibred, exactly as register 256
   only-main: states.
   only-main: The code also carried a constraint the page never stated: obstacle = buildable ⟹ cost ≤ days.
   only-main: Item R refutes it. R — how many closed subsets a closed index has — is buildable, because the
   only-main: enumeration can be written, and unbounded, because counting the closed sets of a closure system is
   only-main: #P-complete (§29). A constraint refuted by its own extent is dead, which is F.3's rule, and it dies
   only-main: here: R occupies a cell the constraint refused. Dropped, the thirteen still close — E(Q) = 0 fibred
   only-main: was never resting on it; only the unfibred count was.
   only-main: At fourteen, fibred and unconstrained, E(Q) = 0 with R as printed above, one claim — the
   only-main: claim being |Cl(ℛ)| for Λ, which §14.5 states as a size. Register 465 entered R as nothing; on
   only-main: that reading the mathematical fibre admits one cell, one claim · buildable · unbounded, which is
   only-main: the cell R now occupies. The later state is on the page, per the register's own rule. Register 465's
   only-main: "the index predicted R" was computed unfibred and unconstrained (E fell 4 to 3) and does not hold
   only-main: under the fibration the appendix asserts; it is withdrawn as a fibred claim and kept as what it
   only-main: was. Register 1729.
   only-main: ### E.2 Closed
