   L8588 ### 30.4.1 And the audit itself was run once
   L8589  The relation set has grown since. Closing the eight polynomial relations the book now states gives a
   L8590  Gröbner basis of 18 where the original four gave 6, and seven further relations reduce to zero that
   L8591  did not before — including V·e = w, w² = (16/3)·T·e and T·h² = eν²/3.
   L8592 
   L8593  Worse, the closure is over polynomial relations only. The book now states at least nine that are not:
   L8594  A^m(x^p) = (−1)^m x^p/(p−1)^m, V = 2/tanh(kh/2), self-concordance, the modular rank law,
   L8595 
   L8596  Σ_q\|A_q\|·\|B_q\| = |Λ|, F(−1) = 2, E(X) as non-pairwise content, and the reorderability theorem. None
   L8597  was ever audited against any list.
